# Commands run by the launchd job com.redwood.demo (see com.redwood.demo.plist).
# What fairplayd changes (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.fairplay, the iOS volume on the flash as the root, where the
# program exists: FLASHBOOT=1, mkjobs.py --root-volume). Two questions, in this order.
#
# First, and it needs no finger: does fairplayd stay up? It wants the IOKit user client
# com_apple_driver_FairPlayIOKitUserClient (its own entitlement names it) and this kernel has no such
# driver, so it may well go the way CommCenter does. "exited due to SIG" in the log answers it.
#
# Second, if it does stay up: the three applications the README blames on its absence. Unlock, then
# App Store, Podcasts and the Weather widget for half a minute each, with `xl screenshot` from another
# terminal while each is open. Icon places are the first home-screen page (docs/homescreen.jpg).
#
# Before the run: do NOT reload the loader as a reflex. The persist copy's resident loader is the main
# line's plus a window for writes into darwin, and it keeps the page's version and size so any kernel reads
# it as its own -- reloading over it stops that copy's runs being able to save, and its note on the phone
# asks you to say so there if you do. Reload only if you have changed xnuloader yourself.
# That said, one boot here did need it and the reason is not settled: with a loader left resident by
# another copy, the kernel got no ufs_shared_pa= on its command line, so its UFS driver never came up,
# /dev/ufs_darwin never appeared ("mount /dev/ufs_darwin: No such file or directory") and the boot fell
# back to /sbin/launchd.ios, which exists only in the RAM image. `./xl reload` with this copy's prebuilt
# loader fixed it immediately. So either that particular resident loader was not the persist one, or the
# "any kernel" claim does not hold for a prebuilt kernel. Check the command line in the log for
# ufs_shared_pa= before reaching for reload. Then
# `./xl ramdisk userland/flashboot.apfs`, then
#   XL_CMDLINE="root_apfs=ufs_darwin ufs=2 ufs_native=1 bootcpu=7 cpus=8 cpufreq=1 touchscreen=1 gpu=1 \
#               adsp=1 wifi=1" XL_SECS=260 ./xl run
# built with CRYPTEXES=flash FLASHBOOT=1 PREBUILT=1 REST=1 RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.fairplay OSLOG=com.apple.fairplayd.H2
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 32 swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 250 wait 10
/bin/ps -A
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.615 0.59 wait 30 button home wait 6
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.385 0.59 wait 30 button home wait 6
/redwood/bin/rwtouch tap 0.27 0.18 wait 30 button home wait 6
/bin/ps -A
